  "question": {
    "text": "The group number, number of valence electrons, and valency of an element with atomic number <math><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo></math> respectively, are:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>15,6</mn></math> and <math><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>16,6</mn></math> and <math><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>16,5</mn></math> and <math><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>15,5</mn></math> and <math><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Atomic number <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> electronic configuration is <br/><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>  <br/>and this element is Phosphorous. <br/>Group no <math><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math>  <br/>Valence <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> present in valence shell <br/><math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>  <br/>Valency <math><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> , it needs <math><mn>3</mn></math> electron to complete its octet."
